{
  "about": "Shared by both settings searches: the desktop one (searchIndex.ts via searchWords.ts) and the phones' (src-tauri/src/services/settings_catalog.rs). filler: words a person types around what they mean ('the setting where ...', 'turn off ...'; a toggle row answers the action itself), dropped unless the whole query is filler; entries with a space are phrases. groups: words people use for the same idea; a typed word in a group also finds rows that use any other word of it, a little below an exact hit. Entries with a space are phrases and are read before filler is dropped ('next to', 'hard to read'). A word sits in one group only. When someone could not find a setting by the words they used, add those words here (or to the row's own aliases) and a case to searchWords.cases.json.",
